{"finding":{"specification":"CipherSpec","message":"the key given to Cipher.init carries a key-origin predicate the rule does not admit","class":"org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey","method":"encrypt","joint_findings":[]},"confirmed_cause":"The reported required-predicate violation is confirmed: the governed AES/GCM Cipher.init receives a caller-supplied key that failed CipherSpec's accepted key-origin predicate in observed executions (CLM-001, CLM-006). The bounded production callers supply either an AndroidKeyStore key or a PBKDF2-derived SecretKey (CLM-004, CLM-005), but the measured runs do not map a failing value to one specific source. Separately, the same AES-GCM initialization supplies only mode and key, while the verified rule requires preparedGCM parameters for GCM; this is an additional required-predicate specification violation. The provider-generated nonce uniqueness question remains unresolved and is not used to dismiss either predicate violation.","plan_invariants":["Existing EncryptedKey records remain decryptable using their persisted transformation string, plaintext-key algorithm identifier, ciphertext, encoded Cipher parameters, and legacy wrapping-key lifecycle (CLM-002, CLM-004, CLM-005).","The plaintext-key algorithm remains authenticated as AAD during encryption, and the same stored algorithm string remains AAD during decryption (CLM-003).","Both bounded production key lifecycles remain supported: AndroidKeyStore-backed use through Encryptor and PBKDF2-derived SecretKey use through MasterKey, including first-use generation and existing persisted data (CLM-004, CLM-005).","Every new AES-GCM record retains its Cipher parameters. The approved prepared-GCM design generates a fresh nonce for each encryption and does not discard legacy parameter decoding (CLM-001, CLM-002).","MasterKey.generate and Encryptor.encryptToken retain their established successful behavior on supported AndroidKeyStore lifecycles; no path supplies caller-generated GCM parameters to a key configuration that rejects them.","EncryptedKey public entry-point names, checked-exception behavior, and existing test-pinned plaintext/ciphertext round-trip expectations remain unchanged.","No verifier format, authentication screen, common verifier API, or emergency action is evidenced by this finding; none is changed by this patch."],"plan_forbidden_changes":["Do not replace the AndroidKeyStore or PBKDF2-derived wrapping keys with an unspecified generated key. The selected lifecycle must define compatible generation, storage, reload, recovery, rotation, and migration behavior.","Do not pass caller-generated GCMParameterSpec values to an AndroidKeyStore key configuration that rejects caller-supplied encryption parameters. The prior regression caused MasterKey.generate and Encryptor.encryptToken to fail with InvalidKeyException after this incompatible change.","Do not remove, reinterpret, or stop persisting the legacy EncryptedKey transformation, plaintext-key algorithm, ciphertext, or encoded Cipher-parameter values, and do not change the existing algorithm-AAD convention.","Do not rename or remove EncryptedKey public entry points, alter their checked-exception propagation, or change existing test expectations to accommodate the migration.","Do not edit unrelated tests, build files, persistence/UI files, or introduce verifier/screen migration behavior not evidenced by this finding."],"adjudication_concerns":[{"kind":"Persisted encrypted-record/key continuity","description":"The patch must preserve decryption of records encrypted with the existing AndroidKeyStore or PBKDF2-derived wrapping-key lifecycle, including records persisted before a change. The representation retains Cipher parameters, but the supplied evidence does not establish a self-describing wrapping-key identity or a legacy-key fallback contract."},{"kind":"Maintainer approval of key-lifecycle semantics","description":"A reviewer must approve the chosen key generation, storage, recovery, rotation, and migration behavior for both production caller paths. This decision is not settled by bounded source evidence or automated validation."},{"kind":"Provider/device GCM behavior","description":"If the review patch makes GCM nonce generation or GCMParameterSpec use explicit, it must be validated on supported Android providers and devices for encryption/decryption interoperability and fresh-nonce behavior. The pipeline does not run instrumentation tests or device/provider checks."}],"co_reported_findings":[],"previous_regressions":["Building the application with the patched Encryptor source.: before, Encryptor.encryptToken called the prior EncryptedKey.encrypt overload, whose declared checked exceptions were all covered by encryptToken's existing throws clause, so this source compiled.; after the patch, Encryptor.encryptToken invokes EncryptedKey.prepareEncryptionCipher, whose declared InvalidAlgorithmParameterException is neither caught nor included in encryptToken's throws clause. Java compilation fails with an unreported checked exception.","Calling Encryptor.encryptToken in the established AndroidKeyStore MASTER-alias lifecycle described in the prior regression, once the checked-exception compilation error is corrected.: before, encryptToken initialized AES/GCM using only the AndroidKeyStore key, allowing the provider to generate the encryption parameters and returning the map containing the encrypted token key.; after the patch, encryptToken supplies a caller-generated 12-byte nonce through GCMParameterSpec to Cipher.init for the existing AndroidKeyStore MASTER key. A key configured with randomized encryption required rejects that initialization with InvalidKeyException, so encryptToken does not return its map.","Calling MasterKey.generate on a supported AndroidKeyStore lifecycle.: before, MasterKey.generate derived the PBKDF2 wrapping key and used the legacy EncryptedKey.encrypt overload, allowing the provider to generate the GCM parameters and completing MasterKey generation.; after the patch, getCurrentWrappingKey creates or reloads currentMasterKey with randomized encryption required, then EncryptedKey.encrypt supplies an explicit caller-generated GCMParameterSpec. AndroidKeyStore rejects that encryption initialization, which is wrapped as InvalidKeyException after the alias may already have been created.","Calling Encryptor.encryptToken in an established lifecycle where the prior masterKey alias allowed the original encryption path.: before, encryptToken resolved masterKey and initialized AES-GCM with only the key, allowing the provider to generate encryption parameters and returning a map containing the encrypted token key.; after the patch, encryptToken creates or reloads currentMasterKey configured with .setRandomizedEncryptionRequired(true), then calls the three-argument EncryptedKey.encrypt overload, which passes a caller-generated nonce in GCMParameterSpec. AndroidKeyStore rejects the initialization and encryptToken throws InvalidKeyException rather than returning the encrypted-key map."],"maintainer_responses_to_this_rule_elsewhere":[],"edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","symbol":"EncryptedKey","original_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;

import android.util.Log;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.AlgorithmParameters;
import java.security.InvalidAlgorithmParameterException;
import java.security.InvalidKeyException;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;

import javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.IllegalBlockSizeException;
import javax.crypto.NoSuchPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

public final class EncryptedKey {
    private final byte[] mCipherText;
    private final byte[] mParameters;
    private final String mCipher;
    private final String mToken;

    private EncryptedKey(Cipher cipher, SecretKey token)
            throws BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        mCipher = cipher.getAlgorithm();
        mToken = token.getAlgorithm();

        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        mCipherText = cipher.doFinal(token.getEncoded());
        mParameters = cipher.getParameters().getEncoded();
    }

    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);
    }

    public SecretKey decrypt(SecretKey key)
            throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException, BadPaddingException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException,
            InvalidKeyException {
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(mCipher);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        String algorithm = cipher.getParameters().getAlgorithm();

        AlgorithmParameters ap = AlgorithmParameters.getInstance(algorithm);
        ap.init(mParameters);

        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, ap);
        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        return new SecretKeySpec(cipher.doFinal(mCipherText), mToken);
    }
}
","corrected_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;

import android.util.Log;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.AlgorithmParameters;
import java.security.InvalidAlgorithmParameterException;
import java.security.InvalidKeyException;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
import java.security.SecureRandom;

import javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.IllegalBlockSizeException;
import javax.crypto.NoSuchPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.GCMParameterSpec;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

public final class EncryptedKey {
    private static final String GCM_TRANSFORMATION = "AES/GCM/NoPadding";
    private static final String GCM_PARAMETERS_ALGORITHM = "GCM";
    private static final int GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS = 128;
    private static final int GCM_NONCE_LENGTH_BYTES = 12;
    private static final int LEGACY_RECORD_VERSION = 0;
    private static final int CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION = 1;
    private static final SecureRandom SECURE_RANDOM = new SecureRandom();

    private final byte[] mCipherText;
    private final byte[] mParameters;
    private final String mCipher;
    private final String mToken;
    private final int mVersion;

    private EncryptedKey(Cipher cipher, SecretKey token)
            throws BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        mCipher = cipher.getAlgorithm();
        mToken = token.getAlgorithm();
        mVersion = CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION;

        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        mCipherText = cipher.doFinal(token.getEncoded());
        mParameters = cipher.getParameters().getEncoded();
    }

    /**
     * Prepares the current record format's AES-GCM encryption cipher for a wrapping key selected
     * by the caller's approved key lifecycle.
     */
    static Cipher prepareEncryptionCipher(SecretKey key)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }

        byte[] nonce = new byte[GCM_NONCE_LENGTH_BYTES];
        SECURE_RANDOM.nextBytes(nonce);

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(GCM_TRANSFORMATION);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key,
                new GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS, nonce));
        return cipher;
    }

    /**
     * Retained public entry point for callers that have not yet prepared a lifecycle cipher.
     */
    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException,
            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException {
        return encrypt(prepareEncryptionCipher(key), plaintext);
    }

    /**
     * Stores a token using a cipher prepared by the caller's approved wrapping-key lifecycle.
     */
    static EncryptedKey encrypt(Cipher cipher, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidKeyException {
        if (cipher == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Cipher is null");
        }
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);
    }

    /**
     * Identifies records whose wrapping key must be resolved through the current lifecycle.
     */
    boolean usesCurrentWrappingKey() {
        return mVersion == CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION;
    }

    /**
     * Returns a defensive copy of the retained Cipher parameters for internal compatibility tests.
     */
    byte[] getEncodedParameters() {
        return (byte[]) mParameters.clone();
    }

    public SecretKey decrypt(SecretKey key)
            throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException, BadPaddingException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException,
            InvalidKeyException {
        if (mVersion != LEGACY_RECORD_VERSION && mVersion != CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION) {
            throw new IOException("Unsupported encrypted key record version: " + mVersion);
        }

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(mCipher);
        AlgorithmParameters parameters = AlgorithmParameters.getInstance(GCM_PARAMETERS_ALGORITHM);
        parameters.init(mParameters);

        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, parameters);
        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        return new SecretKeySpec(cipher.doFinal(mCipherText), mToken);
    }
}
